Z||000000||ocalafiero1||08-25-2001||05:56 PM||||In the never ending saga of my Fiero, I have finally got it running, it idles great. When driving it for the first few miles no problems. Then if I stop at a red light or stop sign, when I accelerate away, it bogs down really bad, and sort of sputters like it going to die, then clears itself up. After another few minutes ( at normal cruise 45 mph 1500-200 rpm) the check engine light comes on until I stop or downshift for traffic. I got home and checked the codes and I'm getting a code 13. The O2 sensor is a new Bosch unit, and is connected. Do you recommend replacing the TPS, if so is there an accurate way of testing it before just buying a new one? I checked the archives and couldn't really find the answer there. Thanks for the help. Btw, the ECM, coil, fuel pump, fuel filter, distributor, ignition module, cap, rotor, wires and plugs are all new and checking out OK. ||||reg||9
Z||000001||theogre||08-25-2001||08:27 PM||||read the wire service article in my cave. A bad O2 ground return would also make the ECM think the sensor is gone.||||reg||1
